# Project structure & build lock

Client-side Vite + React SPA. Deploy target: GitHub Pages at `/performance-rag/`.

## Locked layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `index.vite.html` | **Source of truth** for Vite entry (`/src/main.jsx`). Never delete. |
| `index.html` | May be production HTML on `main` (Pages). Local `npm run dev` / `build` restores it via `scripts/syncIndex.mjs`. |
| `src/` | App code only (`components/`, `context/`, `pages/`, `utils/`). |
| `public/` | Static files copied into `dist` (incl. `sample/`, `.nojekyll`). |
| `docs/`, root `assets/` | **Generated** Pages publish output — do not hand-edit; CI/`npm run build` owns them. |
| `.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml` | Sole deploy path: test → build → publish root + `docs/`. |

Do not invent parallel entrypoints, alternate routers (keep `HashRouter`), or a second deploy workflow unless the user asks.

## Pages / Vite invariants (blank-page bugs)

- Keep `vite.config.js` `base: './'` (relative assets). Do **not** switch to absolute `/performance-rag/` without a deliberate Pages plan.
- Production HTML must reference `./assets/...` — never `/src/main.jsx`.
- After HTML/entry/deploy changes, ensure `index.vite.html` still has the Vite module script for local dev.
- Do not remove root or `docs/.nojekyll` publish steps.

## Build must stay green

Before finishing feature work that touches logic, schema, or tooling:

1. `npm test` (Vitest under `src/**/*.test.js`)
2. `npm run build` (must succeed; `dist/index.html` must not contain `main.jsx`)

If tests or build fail, fix before claiming done. Prefer updating/adding unit tests next to engines (`portfolioEngine`, `analyticsEngine`, `csvSchema`) when changing those modules.

## CSV / sample schema

Roster columns and enums live in `src/utils/csvSchema.js`. Changing schema requires updating `public/sample/` (and `sample/` mirror), generators under `scripts/`, and related tests — do not leave samples or parsers out of sync.

## Git

Follow `no-auto-push.mdc`: commit/push only when the user explicitly asks.
